# 05 — Cleanup, failures and the environment record

<!-- GEN: Why: leftovers poison later runs, silent environment failures look like product bugs, and results without their environment cannot be reproduced. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rules E11, E12, E14 with the workspace's cleanup steps, owners and evidence location. -->

## Cleanup

- Data you created: {{cleanup_data}}
- Processes you started: stop them ({{stop_own_cmd}}); keep the logs for evidence.

## Environment failures

| Failure | Report |
|---|---|
| Service down / unhealthy (not yours) | `BLOCKED` — owner {{stack_owner}} |
| Port conflict you cannot resolve | `BLOCKED` |
| Missing credentials / config | `BLOCKED` — never invent values |
| Provider unavailable, no stub | `BLOCKED` for affected cases |

Never change application code to get past an environment problem.

## Environment record (goes with the results)

```
Revision:   <commit>
Services:   <name@version / url>
Data:       <seed / isolation id>
Stubs:      <provider → tool, or "none">
Accounts:   <role names only>
Started:    <by me | reused>   at <time>
```

